{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/596","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/596/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/596/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/issues/596/events","html_url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/596","id":5859010123,"node_id":"I_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABXTlmSw","number":596,"title":"M7.P5: Resolve the candidate audit — 6 findings (0 critical, 1 high)","user":{"login":"blitterbot","id":335883270,"node_id":"U_kgDOFAUsBg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/335883270?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot","html_url":"https://github.com/blitterbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11946810875,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAACyBXd-w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/labels/audit","name":"audit","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11946810924,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAACyBXeLA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/labels/punch-list","name":"punch-list","color":"5319e7","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/milestones/7","html_url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/milestone/7","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pixelelated/distribution/milestones/7/labels","id":18211751,"node_id":"MI_kwDOMM7sFc4BFeOn","number":7,"title":"M7: pixelelated 0.0.1","description":"## Current priority — M7.P5 browser incident triage, account isolation, and setup clarity\n\nHistorical October9 authorization covered engineering firmware transfers and one reboot each for the RG35XX SP, RG SP and Retroid Pocket Nova, plus the named preparation and screenshot checks. #519's controlled RG35XX SP alignment is ACCEPTED before transfer: exact state-bound receipt, all163 protected files/recovery/credentials preserved, stale experimental records archived and automatic cloud sync disabled. Completed alignment, builds, audits and original-image qualification remain accepted; the next changed image receives its own qualification.\n\nAll three approved transfers, single reboots, installed-artifact checks, preservation comparisons and reviewed compositor frames are COMPLETE. RG35XX SP accepted15:24UTC, RG SP15:54UTC, Nova16:01UTC, followed by final preservation/frame review. Every original stage/reboot result channel is0 and actual owners exited. Both additional devices have been handed back for normal use. Those deployment/build/audit jobs have ended. The #529 VM investigation is complete; its source delta and next-candidate qualification are recorded below. Nova startup observations are retained under #344: one recovered frontend retry also occurs on the prior build; the early SMMU burst is not assigned a cause or frequency. No physical gameplay/audio claim.\n\n### Current work in order\n\nUpdated **2026-10-15 04:35 UTC**. Final source `f8636de1` / ES `16dbac5211eea7e70db7394372033be2be7df829` has artifact, clean-install and retained-upgrade qualification. Native-state proof and final audit closure still precede the next RC/device builds.\n\n1. **Preserve accepted qualification.** Protocol, browser/phone, Wi-Fi, RVZ/proxy, selected account/history, ordinary Wii/Dreamcast saves, and their prior source/image evidence stay accepted in scope. Do not replay completed matrices merely for a new build ID.\n2. **Audit fixes, integration and artifact readback COMPLETE.** All six findings have resolved outcomes; #593, #594 and #595 are closed with final scoped evidence. The actual final image passed 109 installed mappings, GPT, and raw/update SYSTEM+KERNEL equality. #597 is closed: reviewed recovery preserves the original producer reporting failure and unknown launcher wait. A separate artifact reader completed with original zero outcomes; no missing receipt was fabricated. GENERIC_X64 omits the ARM Steam installer, so ARM payload readback remains a device-build check.\n3. **Affected clean-install and retained-upgrade checks COMPLETE.** Both passed selected state and three installed-loader checks, four installed Dolphin helper transitions, and actual installed ES Wi-Fi Back/reopen/normal exit. Back upper bounds57.909324ms and57.258077ms. Normal retained update changed boot ID, preserved eight selected paths/bytes/modes, and left its protected base unchanged. Complete original outcomes and reviewed frames are published in `0ca9443280`.\n4. **Finish four-launch native-state continuation NOW.** Native01 stopped before any game launch because its fixture required an explicit global Off key that ES removes during normal serialization. Preserve that original failure and partial-export limits. Review the narrow source-proven fixture correction, then use a fresh isolated owner to verify Wii manual state restoration and Dreamcast manual/automatic state behavior. No clean/retained, ordinary-save or broad-matrix replay.\n5. **Complete #596/#590 acceptance, then #555 H700 followed by SM8550.** Finish audit/cadence records only after native evidence exists. Rebind device plans to the final published source and fresh custody/capacity checks; both targets have changed kernel inputs, while SM8550 also needs current FEX Nix-input proof and ABL1.2 checks. Old carry-forward assertions cannot be reused unchanged. Review candidate list/upstream queue before builds. Physical transfer/reboot still requires the relevant owner authorization.\n\n**Accepted scope:** normal proxy main/systemd lifecycle, native ISO/RVZ component checks, independent Dolphin conversion, CHD parity, Steam caller/recovery controls, browser memory handoff and setup frames remain evidence for their exact inputs. A fresh native proxy library is now built from the three current source pins and bound into the successful startup test. Final installed/native integration is still distinct from those component results. The prior English640 and French help/refusal frames are complete; new #594 error-branch frames are now verified at both panel sizes; final native-state qualification remains due as listed above.\n\n**Owner choices retained:** stable20261001 foundation, normal explicit cloud folder selection without automatic movement, interim shared ScreenScraper developer identity (D-WORKFLOW-166), and upstream submissions only after the initial current build (#585/D-WORKFLOW-165). #558 shutdown recurrence and #561 LED preference remain watches; #586 replacement developer identity, #568 progress wording, #562 ROM integrity, #560 fast shutdown, #587 browser-owned proxy suspension and #576 GTK4 are backlog, not extra RC gates. Native lazy-import savings were only390KiB; no production migration is selected.\n\n**Tracking and execution:** docs/releases/next-candidate-work.md is the dated readiness table; this milestone body owns order. Three visible Herdr lanes encountered sign-in refresh failures and are not claimed active. Explicit internal source workers continue under coordinator ownership; runtime/compiler allocations remain serialized and actively supervised. No off-session notifier is claimed. No known defect is waived to call an RC.\n\n**Historical October13 browser controls (complete; runtime status superseded above):** Record published in `93e64677f33c0a9dae9f8539903188780da02f04`, both exact-head hosted checks successful and delivery owners exited0.  All22 shared-VM controls are COMPLETE: six synthetic normal-ES-handoff phone trials, eight actual unauthenticated rclone Dropbox user-agent trials and eight CSS-width trials. All measured cases loaded and returned, with original launcher/wrapper/build0 and owner exits; setup failures remain recorded. Current handset UA selects fallback provider bundles and the alternatives modern bundles; repeated desktop trials are more consistently responsive but do not resolve memory pressure. Narrower layouts offer no consistent benefit; zoom changes CSS height/DPR too. Cookie overlay remains, so this is not completed login/input acceptance. Compact packets: docs/qa-logs/2026-10-13-browser-handoff/, 2026-10-13-dropbox-user-agents/ and 2026-10-13-dropbox-breakpoints/. The shared VM/disk/keys are retired,2,362,486,784 allocated bytes recovered; no browser runtime or firmware build remains active.\n\n**Historical parallel feasibility and component test complete October13 (runtime status superseded above):** pix-memory returned f1987b6 +914b0ad; all source/fixture hashes and historical receipts were independently checked. A fresh VM20 with installed Python3.14.7 measured only390KiB (0.38MiB) median PSS savings in six bytecode imports, versus the earlier5442KiB host-source result. Two synthetic source-module loopback probes pass cached login/next-game readiness, signed award/DB preservation and401 passthrough. This is component proof, not full-service/ES or device savings. All watched channels0/exited; VM/disk/keys retired,2,244,435,968allocated bytes recovered. pix-gtk4 returned da0ecd8 +10f9b16: exact dependency/API/native-keyboard constraints and a static compiler process-group cleanup correction; no GTK4 build/runtime result. Both source-only lanes completed; no test/build is active. D-WORKFLOW-163 retains both directions as diagnostic-only and prioritizes actual-page CPU/script versus reclaim/input-to-paint attribution. GTK4 requires a separately allocated dependency/API/keyboard spike; it is not an unconditional migration gate. #493 still precedes full cache copies/builds. Evidence is integrated in the coordinator branch under docs/qa-logs/2026-10-13-proxy-memory-feasibility/, 2026-10-13-proxy-memory-vm/ and 2026-10-13-gtk4-feasibility/; Record published at `1a37cde40ab0893c9c21c0a383c59ac0c1403b06`; both exact-head hosted checks passed, all delivery03 channels0 and owners exited. The refused delivery02 remains preserved; no published history was rewritten. M7's remaining ordered steps are unchanged.\n\n**Historical October12 checkpoint (superseded by October13 below):** Source intake and prior record delivery are complete. Diagnostic evidence is published at `d4f0ed282411e113995789b8eae5d6a0de2c693c` with both hosted record/wordlist checks successful; feature/m7-player-setup and next were clean at that commit. The diagnostic source base was515cd8e79a; the stable20261001 foundation stays isolated until #564 is repaired. #570's nine-case low-memory VM matrix and explicitly approved bounded H700 WebKit probe are COMPLETE and retired. Public login reaches the physical memory guard at34s; closing restores572MiB available. Older application/current engine, UA/cache changes, supplied GStreamer payload and accelerated VM graphics do not materially reduce memory. All runs use WebKit2.54.1; an older-engine runtime comparison and repeated navigation/input/ES-handoff/recovery proof are next. #572 has failure1/supplied-success0 plugin controls but still needs a real recipe/package repair. Evidence: docs/qa-logs/2026-10-12-browser-isolation/. No product fix, full image build, external audit or account/cloud operation occurred; no test is left running.\n\n**October13 #570/#572 diagnostic checkpoint:** Rule, package repair and evidence are published in `2292e9a2983227a62aaf7846a5b739c41b0841a7`; both exact-head hosted checks passed and delivery01 exited0. #573 is closed completed. WebKit2.54.0 isolated package rebuild is COMPLETE. Initial loaded low-memory trials put both engines near390MiB PSS; repeated1024MiB launches stall with both2.54.0 and2.54.1, then reset the guest during2.54.0. Original matrix remains FAILED; reset cause is unproved.2048MiB headroom controls load both engines with zero direct reclaim; no downgrade rationale. Actual #572 recipe/install/fresh-registry negative-success controls and warning-free browser proof pass, while final assembled-image closure remains open. D-WORKFLOW-162/#573 requires early dated upstream issue/release/fix checks; latest WebKit stable remains2.54.1, no confirmed upstream match. All test owners exited and VM/disk/keys retired; no build/test running. Evidence: docs/qa-logs/2026-10-13-webkit-versions/. Next: whole-process/kernel/GPU accounting and normal ES handoff, matched browser acceleration controls with actual renderer evidence, and H700-specific corroboration; then the earlier2.52.6 boundary with configuration controls. Continue #565→#566→#567→#571 and the remaining ordered gates afterward. No new firmware, owner-device/cloud operation or production WebKit pin change.\n\n**October13 browser-stack controls COMPLETE:** Eight bounded RG35XX SP controls,5reviewed frames, whole-process/kernel/DRM samples and all three original launcher/wrapper/build/exited-owner receipts are recorded at docs/qa-logs/2026-10-13-browser-stack/. The owner named this separate handheld as the browser bench (D-QA-060); RG SP remains off. Simple off/on loads use134/164MiB PSS; final public on/off both load and still guard-stop. Unequal truncated peaks are not an efficiency comparison; earlier pre-load stops remain incomplete. Same boot/frontend/proxy/compositor, recovered headroom, all browser processes gone and temporary device outputs retired. No saves/game/account/cloud/firmware/reboot action. Existing proxy handles reconnect uploads and optional background work but is not a browser dependency; safely reducing its resident cost needs synthetic queue/readiness/recovery proof, not an owner-service toggle. Next #570: normal ES handoff/navigation/input/return and complete resource accounting, including VM proxy lifecycle/idle-footprint controls; then2.52.6 boundary. No production fix or root cause established, no test left running. Record/bench authorization published in `d29d0781ecb416ed8d51323b1fa2c3237755b8ff`; both exact-head hosted checks pass, delivery launcher/wrapper/build0 and actual owners exited. Main/feature are clean. No diagnostic/build job remains running.\n\nThe numbered items below retain the completed predecessor and monitoring state; they are not proof for the new foundation.\n\n1. **#548 / #344 — corrected GENERIC_X64 qualification COMPLETE.** Frozen source `1a026648442321609b2288c2c9c06803817f9df2`, identity `0.0.1-dev+20261011T194522Z.g1a0266484423`, ES `c8dc72cf9e`, immutable bundle `bd85b1b42f0170d7d82555af09cbe18762d6fc7eae63293bd0a8043e652db548`. Installed payload, clean startup,14 standard suites/78-frame comparison,108 each WebDAV/SFTP/S3,8 reviewed clean/retained INFORMATION frames and real19→20 upgrade pass. Four save hashes/settings/selection/path/backup survive; retained fresh/108WebDAV/exit/time-to-play pass. Upgrade20 ends0 at20:39:38UTC and all owners/guests/endpoints exited. Original QA20 remains1 for7host-harness failures; final #550/#551 correction passes1378checks/0failures/0skips against the same source. #552 strict acceptance02 ends0, retaining its original parser failure. Explicit composed qualification, never a rewritten original result.\n2. **#553 / #554 — independent review and all repairs COMPLETE.** One approved Fable5.1/xhigh call ended0 at21:49:17UTC with verified provenance. All13 leads were adjudicated; four evidence/tool/comment repairs are verified and published in9f170ee741. Both issues are closed completed, with exact checked-body readbacks and a valid audit-completion marker. Primary44PASS/5existing528PARTIAL; no confirmed product runtime defect. Completion commitbc9dfe8141 is published: full local ceremony and both exact-head hosted checks are green; delivery owner ended0 at22:19:33UTC and exited. No repeated external transfer.\n3. **#557 — RG SP/Nova updates COMPLETE.** Both RG SP and Nova updates are COMPLETE. Both full device transfer hashes, one approved reboot each, installed firmware/boot-chain/native checks and private preservation comparisons pass. All original stage/reboot result channels are0 and actual owners exited. Both run bc9dfe8141 / 0.0.1-dev+20261011T222153Z.gbc9dfe8141d9, frontend active with NRestarts0 and automatic cloud sync off. RG SP163 files/25,545,421bytes plus5 recovery entries are unchanged. Nova configured safe scope is empty; credentials/paths/all settings values are unchanged, though system.cfg bytes were rewritten. Both returned through Tailnet and are handed back to owner use. No personal-cloud operation, screenshot, game or injected input occurred; RG35XX SP remains untouched. Compact acceptance is published at docs/qa-logs/2026-10-12-owner-updates/; #557 is closed completed after exact-head verification.\n4. **#493 — both approved cleanup batches COMPLETE.** All17 additional superseded worktrees removed at05:05:58UTC; original channels/launcher0, actual exits, source/record/current-cache post-checks and acceptance consumed. Recovered1.98TB; filesystem now has3.02TB available. Original branches, current three caches (~446GB), accepted firmware and required source/compact evidence retained. First64-target cleanup is separately complete. Neither may be replayed. Remaining exact recovery-payload retirement stays under#493/#555. Mandatory launch admission is now delivered; every new copy/compile needs its own current measured receipt. Automatic retirement/reconciliation and D-INFRA-023 actual-build resource telemetry remain open. No hardware change is selected; #563 defines the next candidate.\n5. **#558 — Nova normal-shutdown recurrence: nonblocking watch, read-only triage COMPLETE, cause unresolved.** October13 owner confirms normal shutdown and unplugging external power during shutdown before restart; no new Linux-load error or repeated loop is established. Retained power-off requests at11:01:10 and11:17:01EDT, the former followed by Linux boot11seconds later; exact owner-time mapping is not yet established. Three reads0/exited; pstore empty, named reason paths absent, source power-off routing confirmed, upstream charging behavior only a lead. New sanitized packet: docs/qa-logs/2026-10-13-nova-shutdown/. No reproduction or device mutation. October12 packet/afb6cb4ef7 record is historical; #557 remains completed.\n6. **#561 — RG SP LED preference: monitor during owner use and subsequent upgrades.** The owner selected Default; readback confirms no saved override, green1/red0. Initial source/read-only investigation is published in0fc5a41e99 with successful checks and consumed original results. Original writer remains unknown. At the owner's direction, retain this as a keep-an-eye-on item, with the unrun H700 VM interruption matrix deferred; it is not an active pre-next-image gate. The persistent-setter lead remains unproved. Recurrence or a reproduced VM defect resumes investigation before any proposed fix. Preserve Default; no device LED mutation or reproduction is authorized.\n7. **#528 / #344 / #265 / #337 / #359 — publication completion.** Engineering component dispositions are delivered, retaining all capabilities. Shader/ABL aggregate terms, vendor/prebuilt/source coverage, final-image inventory, independent retrieval/off-host custody, bot/runner readback, adoption/recovery/support/SSH/cloud/source notes, channel separation, per-asset physical smoke and named publication authority still hold publication. Public naming remains0.0.1-rc.N then0.0.1; no RC allocated here.\n\nReplacement19 qualification is complete for its own source: standard/protocol with explicitly composed fixes, real retained upgrade/save hashes, clean/retained connection controls, public ROCKNIX configuration preservation, native/service/consent/USB checks,22 reviewed UI/startup frames and actual same-model/foreign archive/manual-folder proof. #531 and #541–547 are closed; original failing aggregates remain unchanged. The newer image20 runtime proof above is also complete. [Installed UI/startup evidence](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/tree/3fcff2e1e2f9c8502e04180a5db2036bd4016497/docs/qa-logs/2026-10-11-installed-ui).\n\n**#533 reconciliation:** the original18 open M7 issues and four bugs were mapped; new #535–#539 and audit #540 are dispositioned above; #537 is closed with the completed combined-image qualification above. #534 is a preserved fixed LED-color selection, with read-only diagnosis recorded; #535 open-network password handling is source/VM-qualified and closed. #352 delivered; #353 automatic migration retired; #510 qualified; #354 consolidated into #344. #350 exact-image proof is complete; #349 public docs remain under #511; #395 moves to explicit backlog, while active supervision remains mandatory. Full disposition, original contract mapping, exact proposed pins, source-bound evidence, watcher and retirement plan: [next candidate scope](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/next/docs/releases/next-candidate-scope.md).\n\n**Completed prior device work:** #519 alignment and the October9 transfers/reboots/readbacks remain complete. The October11 RG35XX SP authority under #556 is now consumed and accepted; all devices are in owner use.\n\n**Parallel #511:** website/setup/ROM/BIOS guides stay in their separate Herdr lane; startup trust remains that lane's question. Local instructions work without a live site. **Personal #516:** optional residue cleanup remains separate; no bulk cloud cleanup or first sync is implied. #519 no longer awaits approval or execution.\n\n## Completed qualification — retain, do not rerun\n\n- **#510/#515/#520/#521/#522/#523:** settled post-rclone contract and finite layout disposition; preserve selected independent paths, no automatic cloud-folder move/follow. Source, target-native capture dependencies, explicit modes and reviewed flow/frame references are published. Unsupported ROM/BIOS layouts retain instructions. Linking a backend is not relocation consent (D-CLOUD-175/176/178/179).\n- **#507/#524:** independent primary plus both approved Fable5.1/xhigh reviews, all four fixes, resolution evidence and exact-head hosted checks completed; both issues closed. Earlier candidate16 audit #471 also remains complete. Do not repeat external transfers.\n- **#508/#526/#527:** final source/installed CF10/public-configuration preservation and real retained-storage upgrade are qualified. Replacement18 has13 unaffected standard suites plus separately qualified corrected walks and composed78-frame comparison. The original qa-21 aggregate rc1 remains unchanged; this is composed qualification, not a relabelled original run. WebDAV/SFTP/S3 each108 assertions (324total); candidate16→18 upgrade31checks. All16 corrected frames reviewed at640×480/1280×800; no baseline or blanket-mask change. Source/canonical flow/EN-FR branch evidence is retained.\n- **#492:** H70002 and SM855003 engineering firmware and final inventories accepted; issue closed. Both use distribution `8b5113fa164ada7d002ab138b1e3a9bf795e9de5` and ES `1d76b3da7da75794066df1c089931b890304da7a`. H700 ARM244/aarch64671 and SM8550 ARM245/aarch64737 tasks completed. All original final build/acceptance channels0, actual owners/container exited. Original failed attempts remain failures. Those qualification jobs are complete; #529 is a separate startup investigation.\n\nQualification: [replacement18](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/next/docs/qa-logs/2026-10-08-pixelelated-replacement-18/qualification.md), [corrected walks](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/tree/next/docs/qa-logs/2026-10-08-cloud-folder-walks), [device artifacts](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/tree/next/docs/qa-logs/2026-10-08-device-refresh), [final inventories](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/tree/next/docs/qa-logs/2026-10-08-final-inventory).\n\n## Previous firmware and source custody — historical basis\n\nH70002 bundle `1b93642b24901b5c3a96b0a079d6fb4486ca30d213b4b2db890c6e3630404175`; TAR `b49cca4ca0b8996fa994181508c887d9df5afe155c9502919bab7bf7e153e39d`. Both DDR variants/update bytes,185 ARM handoff files, native helpers/catalog/post-update/identity pass.\n\nSM855003 bundle `afcb966f246118798c87e59cd5bc6ce7c2c21167a5d712faea56393409d9d79d`; TAR `b3f1a8190e04abbf64d35486601ee19fce35d2d25bc7239b1be7cccd9fb43730`. Raw/update equality, GPT, all5 ABL files,187 ARM handoff files and14 FEX outputs pass. Two changed ARM outputs in each build differ only in bounded embedded revision/date/time strings; exact new bytes were accepted.\n\nAll2,327 component/profile rows (701 distinct components) map to local retained inputs:605 exact archives/9.04GB,372 Git snapshots,43 roots,439 submodule edges, frozen distribution recipes/patches and separately retained prebuilt sources. Only Teakra's unused test LFS payload is omitted with explicit source/build-edge disposition. This inventory is not complete corresponding-source/licence clearance.\n\nThe current notice basis is `docs/qa-logs/2026-10-09-notice-scope/licence-basis-corrected.json`.13of17 have some root/scoped evidence, not13 cleared components. GLSL's LGPL notice belongs to nnedi3, not the entire collection. Common/GLSL/RetroPie/slang shaders and ABL lack an established aggregate basis. rclone's embedded revision matches retained source but reports modified=true; Tailscale's version/tag evidence is not a reproducible-binary proof. ABL packaging is not implementation source; LinuxLoader `4588733123554b1f7bf935b04e494e4284894546` returned404 to blitterbot. Owner source/contact question remains pending; no upstream outreach occurred. IntendedB2 remains subject to the owner's comparison (D-WORKFLOW-107); no bucket or purchase inferred.\n\n## Phase map and naming\n\n| Phase | State | Evidence/remaining boundary |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| M7.P0 — Tracking conventions | COMPLETE | #388/#389; milestone body is the ordered queue and open titles follow it. |\n| M7.P1 — Safe migration and recovery | Historical source gate complete; folder move/follow superseded by #508 | #365/#356/#320/#391/#392 proofs retained. Settings recovery/locking remain required. |\n| M7.P2 — Qualified release inputs | COMPLETE | #361/#362/#386, #310/#327/#332 software gates; proxy/dependencies and cut-time freshness retained. |\n| M7.P3 — Build and qualify | COMPLETE software qualification | Candidate16 plus final replacement18 composed qualification; exact manifests, failure controls and upgrade/provider/frame receipts. |\n| M7.P4 — Independent fixes audit | COMPLETE | #471 and later #507/#524 independent receipts; no repeat needed. |\n| M7.P5 — Device and release completion | IN PROGRESS | Ordered work above; accepted firmware, authorized physical updates, remaining #528 and release/publication gates. |\n\nM7-wide umbrellas #383/#344 omit P; #354 is consolidated. Other open titles use their owning phase. #344's historical contract P0–P6 headings are contract sections, not this execution queue. Closed titles stay historical. Prior migration-copy #502/#504/#505 evidence is superseded by #508, not authority to resume cloud migration. The complete prior milestone body is retained in the deployment tracking packet.\n\n## Explicitly outside this release\n\nInfrastructure topology/restore drill #347/#348/#355; replacement runner/inherited-code review #336/#339/#346; general audit-depth policy #378; reusable upstream integration/backport procedure #559 (D-WORKFLOW-116/117 cadence settled; the concrete20261001 intake is now #563 under D-WORKFLOW-161) and fast-shutdown/metadata evaluation #560; device telemetry #387 and FOSS build-observability evaluation #432; disconnected notifications #395; RA fixture reset automation #464/#240; optional Dropbox/offsite QA #463; ROM/cloud byte-integrity comparison #562; temporary offline-proxy shutdown during browser use #587 (conditional lifecycle/memory experiment, D-RA-047); active-name cleanup #509; personal redundancy #518; broader site/trademark work. Existing release custody requirements still apply. D-INFRA-022 retains only immediate-test payloads plus durable compact evidence and required source custody. No RC designation or public publication clearance is claimed.\n\n\n### Owner testing feedback — October12\n\n#565, #566 and #567 were initially filed as future tasks and are now in the ordered M7.P5 queue at the owner's explicit request. #568 final-game/finalization progress remains future work; it asks which phase is running, not for an owner copy decision. #586 replacement ScreenScraper credentials are also future work; #566 interim selection is settled by D-WORKFLOW-166. #569 tracks sanitized configuration diagnosis; private incident evidence stays private. Prior accepted firmware and closed qualification remain evidence for their original source only.\n\n\n### Historical October13 allocator diagnostic — source status superseded above\n\nThe allocator and clean-state investigations are published at `e398cbb9977e29173616a067c0e26b09e09e7ba2`. #570's four valid actual Dropbox handoff trials returned 77.64/75.73 MiB of ES anonymous memory in 2.049/2.018 ms, versus zero for both shams. This is a diagnostic interposer result; the source proposal was then UNCOMPILED. That status is superseded by the published compiled candidate and bounded smoke above; the actual-binary comparison and bounded repeated lifecycle are now complete above; remaining success/failure and broader UI qualification is current. No pin change or physical fix claim. Source-only WebKit policy and GTK4 alternatives are held; prior proxy target savings were only390KiB.\n\n#565 now has an executable selected account/cloud/history/QA gate and prepare-only release integration: actual ready fresh VM20 PASS0,113 guest controls PASS0,142 host root/payload/release-preparation controls PASS0. Original failures are preserved. Final gate differs from guest proof only in empty_ext4; composed qualification is explicit. Actual next firmware payload and genuine retained-storage upgrade remain due. Nova's September29 install retained storage; September30 empty restore/0B backup explain activity stamps, and pre-install play metadata explains Recent membership. Account/history original entry remains unknown; no owner reset or cleanup occurred.\n\nThose two historical diagnostic owners and their temporary disks/UEFI/keys were retired; this is not the current runtime status described above. [Memory and provenance evidence](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/e398cbb9977e29173616a067c0e26b09e09e7ba2/docs/qa-logs/2026-10-13-memory-state-followup/README.md), [clean-state qualification](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/blob/e398cbb9977e29173616a067c0e26b09e09e7ba2/docs/qa-logs/2026-10-13-clean-state-runtime/README.md). The remaining M7 order above is unchanged; #493 admission is delivered and must be used for new copies/builds. Automatic cleanup remains separately open. No new RC or publication clearance.","creator":{"login":"blitterbot","id":335883270,"node_id":"U_kgDOFAUsBg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/335883270?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot","html_url":"https://github.com/blitterbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blitterbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":24,"closed_issues":199,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-09-30T23:52:54Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T05:16:17Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-10-15T02:27:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T05:16:17Z","closed_at":"2026-10-15T05:16:17Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# M7 independent audit punch list\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe independent audit examined the M7 delta, retaining explicit baseline exclusions and distinguishing actual installed artifacts from helper, source-chroot and private-candidate controls. It derived every criterion before opening prior per-criterion verdicts. Source, original command/child results, selected before/after identities, databases and UI frames support substantial preservation and recovery behavior. Later evidence now verifies the named native manual and automatic save-state cases. Accepted synthetic matrices and ordinary cold game-save proof were preserved at their original source/scope without replay.\n\nSix audit findings survive: one High (F-002 NoGUI achievement lifecycle), three Medium (F-001 metadata bounds, F-003 missing Sys resources, G-02 stale retained achievement settings), and two Low (G-01 normal ES scan shutdown, G-03 runtime Python isolation). The first three have later landed corrections and independently checked bounded runtime evidence. PL-006 resolves at committed source d9054efc after exact installed-interpreter controls; its unchanged source is now also bound into final f863 artifacts, without a native ARM claim. PL-004 resolves after original helper controls and full EN/FR refusal flow at640/1280. PL-005 resolves after exact published ES16dbac/distribution pin342eec and original normal-exit/Back/reopen proof. Final f863 clean/retained continuations verify both installed corrections within their selected scope. Native-state qualification is now independently accepted within the exact four-launch scope in native-state02-readback.md.\n\nBoth pinned Anthropic Fable5.1/xhigh calls completed through the Facilitator with matching prompts/output digests, provider-response model identity and original successful channels. Every blind/refutation lead was checked against source/originals. The external reviewer received no pixels and only attested summaries for later image receipts; primary visual/original readback remains separately identified. Native03 ordinary Wii/Dreamcast cold game-save evidence is independently consumed. Later f863 originals now verify completed Wii/Flycast manual restore, global-On/native-Off preservation and native-On/global-Off save/cold restore; the historical criterion score remains frozen. See native-gameplay-supplement-readback.md for preserved exporter failure and additive full byte verification. Primary exact model identity remains unverified; OpenAI lab and Codex harness are known.\n\n\n**Audit outcome:** all seven phases complete; six findings resolved. Final selected clean/retained and named native-state originals accepted on f863/ES16dbac. Frozen score and original failures are preserved. This is not RC or blanket hardware approval.\n\n## Task checklist\n\n- [x] PL-001 — Initialize and shut down achievements in DolphinNoGUI; Resolved in `9aaaaa0f642b97ebf722c2e1aeedb7e4d00bcbdc`, present in d4af and next by direct branch/read checks. `dolphin-installed-supplement-readback.md` verifies original installed evidence. G-02 is a separate retained-settings defect, not a reason to erase this lifecycle correction.\n- [x] PL-002 — Bound Proton release metadata requests; Resolved in `9aaaaa0f642b97ebf722c2e1aeedb7e4d00bcbdc`; exact metadata control/readback in `steam-supplement-readback.json` and durable Steam remaining result. Undeclared-length size enforcement is not claimed; total time remains bounded. No installed ARM Steam claim.\n- [x] PL-003 — Supply Dolphin resources at its compiled immutable Sys path; Resolved in `6616cc36cb85d86878870feafdcb64edbc192df8` under #592, present in d4af/next; engineering-image and dolphin-installed supplemental readbacks directly verify originals. No claim every Sys consumer was separately exercised.\n- [x] PL-004 — Clear retained Dolphin achievements when disabled or signed out; Resolved in `d9054efc463387df3f0211481c5ae8c793dfadc8` on feature/m7-player-setup under #594. All15 helper/exact caller-block controls plus actual full Wii/runemu/ES intended EN/FR refusal at640/1280 and exact original config restoration verified (audit-ui1280-02-readback.md). Those flow controls used explicit candidate overlays. Final f863 untouched/retained continuations additionally verify actual installed full helper/exact launcher blocks with synthetic engine markers, source-preservation checks and original exits; see final-clean-affected-readback.md and final-retained-affected-readback.md.\n- [x] PL-005 — Cancel and join the Wi-Fi scan worker at normal ES exit; Resolved in published ES `16dbac5211eea7e70db7394372033be2be7df829`, pinned by distribution `342eec66e9fc510f6defc87de1131d300d2e804c`. Original syntax/link/driver controls, actual baseline/candidate normal exit and candidate Back/reopen verify;59.060466ms complete-frame upper bound, same blocked group/one enumeration, no candidate forced cleanup or survivors (wifi-back-reopen-readback.md, phase7-publication-readback.json). Original failed suites remain. Final f863 clean/retained originals additionally show actual installed ES Back57.909324/57.258077ms, same blocked group/one enumeration, normal SIGINT join and no candidate forced cleanup or survivors; final-clean-affected-readback.md and final-retained-affected-readback.md. SIGTERM/fatal behavior remains outside this guarantee.\n- [x] PL-006 — Isolate the Steam runtime Python invocation; Resolved in `d9054efc463387df3f0211481c5ae8c793dfadc8` on feature/m7-player-setup. Exact installed-interpreter old-negative/candidate-positive full synthetic runtime controls pass; source-controls02-readback.md. Exact source blobs are unchanged in final f863 and the109-row artifact reader binds its installed source; see phase7-final-image-source-readback.json and supplements/image-reader02-result/auditor-review.json. No native ARM execution claim.\n\n# M7 next candidate audit punch list\n\nScope: independent Milestone audit #590; frozen distribution fac608ff89940ce358ea9b8a95e9a08a6fe26568 and ES3178b832b8d134198b2b4eede4f725d4ed283f8c. Two verified Fable5.1/xhigh passes plus the primary OpenAI perspective, all leads independently graded. This is not a council or RC approval.\n\nSix audit-discovered findings: 0 Critical, 1 High, 3 Medium, 2 Low. All six have committed, narrowly verified corrections. Final selected clean/retained composition and the named four-launch native-state proof on f863/ES16dbac are independently accepted; the audit cycle is complete within its declared scope. Exact source/blob and artifact readback binds PL-006 into f863, while installed controls remain synthetic and no native ARM claim is made. Frozen/current-audit score: 80 PASS, 16 PARTIAL, 16 SKIP, 3 FAIL, 0 UNTESTABLE of115. Original pre-external score remains in pre-external-scorecard.json. Later source fixes do not rewrite frozen behavior.\n\nAll discovered items have recorded resolved outcomes. Root owns final tracker/artifact publication and the separately tracked device/release work. No broad accepted matrix must be repeated merely to improve audit prose. Each acceptance states the bounded proof needed; preserve original failed observations and explicitly distinguish source proposal, private candidate and installed artifact.\n\nAudit scope/intake: #590. Mandatory Phase6 punch tracker: [#596](https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/596), created by root from exact reviewed body bytes and independently read back. Scheduled title follows canonical M7.P5 naming; labels audit/punch-list and milestone7 verified. Source follow-ups #592/#593/#594/#595 link the concrete corrections; the punch checklist remains authoritative for audit resolution.\n\n## PL-001: Initialize and shut down achievements in DolphinNoGUI\n\n- **Severity:** High\n- **Category:** Interaction Defect\n- **Source Finding:** F-002\n- **Owner area:** Dolphin package / default frontend\n- **What:** Supply the lifecycle missing from the default frontend while preserving disabled and failed-boot cleanup.\n- **Where:** projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/standalone/dolphin-sa/patches/018-nogui-achievements-lifecycle.patch\n- **Why:** Correct INI and a compile flag cannot enable a client that was never constructed; AC102 fails on frozen fac608.\n- **Evidence:** Original installed baseline logs the null-client error with enabled=true, initialized=0 and no requests. Complete frozen source shows Qt-only lifecycle. Later installed d4af ELF5cb5dac has original enabled/disabled/failed-boot exits0/0/1 and lifecycle1/1,0/0,1/1.\n- **Acceptance:** Land the guarded lifecycle patch, compile the actual target, and retain original actual-installed enabled/disabled/failed-boot lifecycle and loopback request/cleanup evidence. No real login, award or gameplay inference.\n\n## PL-002: Bound Proton release metadata requests\n\n- **Severity:** Medium\n- **Category:** Code Quality\n- **Source Finding:** F-001\n- **Owner area:** Steam installer\n- **What:** Put -q first and retain finite connect/total/response-size limits on the two top-level release metadata requests.\n- **Where:** projects/ROCKNIX/packages/virtual/emulators/sources/Install Steam.sh:213\n- **Why:** Exited Python child alarms do not cover this shell curl; a stalled server can keep foreground installation waiting. AC083 fails on frozen source.\n- **Evidence:** Full caller/source trace plus original installed-curl candidate controls: normal0/0, declared-size oversize63, stall28 at30.006s and function failure after its existing10s message delay; no forced cleanup or unexpected requests.\n- **Acceptance:** Land the bounded exact function and preserve installed curl/Bash normal, declared-size oversize and stalled-response originals, exact argv, family-state equality and child cleanup.\n\n## PL-003: Supply Dolphin resources at its compiled immutable Sys path\n\n- **Severity:** Medium\n- **Category:** Interaction Defect\n- **Source Finding:** F-003\n- **Owner area:** Dolphin package installation\n- **What:** Install the immutable relative Sys alias without moving resources into retained storage.\n- **Where:** projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/standalone/dolphin-sa/package.mk\n- **Why:** Compiled /usr/share/dolphin-emu/sys is absent while resources live in /usr/config/dolphin-emu; badges, approved lists and global configuration consumers share the root.\n- **Evidence:** Frozen staged path missing and original private candidate badge loads fail. Later d4af image six resource paths match pinned source hashes and resolve inside read-only squashfs; all12 historical badge-error counts are0 across three actual installed startup cases.\n- **Acceptance:** Land the package alias, pass package checks/build, and retain exact installed link/resource identities plus absence of the four previous badge failures across enabled, disabled and boot-error startup controls.\n\n## PL-004: Clear retained Dolphin achievements when disabled or signed out\n\n- **Severity:** Medium\n- **Category:** Interaction Defect\n- **Source Finding:** G-02 (external R-01)\n- **Owner area:** Dolphin helper and both native launchers\n- **What:** Atomically publish an explicitly inactive credential-free INI for both negative states, and refuse native launch if publication fails.\n- **Where:** projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/standalone/dolphin-sa/scripts/cheevos_dolphin.sh:21\n- **Why:** Early1 leaves prior Enabled=True/token/hardcore/host intact; launchers continue. Already affects Qt and becomes active on default NoGUI after the lifecycle repair. AC100 FAIL, AC101 PARTIAL.\n- **Evidence:** Complete source/package search confirms sole writer and unchecked caller exits; pinned manager reads retained settings. No authentication success is assumed. Correction d9054efc passes all15 actual guest source controls and full Wii/runemu/ES intended EN/FR refusal at640 and1280 with exact original restoration (source-controls02-readback.md, audit-ui02-readback.md, audit-ui1280-02-readback.md).\n- **Acceptance:** Two seeded-enabled-state transitions produce disabled/blank outputs with expected original1 and unchanged source settings. Failed publication preserves prior bytes and prevents both engines from launching with original error status; unchanged enabled routing and narrow EN/FR refusal flow/frame proof retained.\n\n## PL-005: Cancel and join the Wi-Fi scan worker at normal ES exit\n\n- **Severity:** Low\n- **Category:** Code Quality\n- **Source Finding:** G-01 (external F-12b)\n- **Owner area:** ES Wi-Fi worker lifecycle\n- **What:** Retain application lifetime ownership and cooperative cancellation, then join before frontend/log teardown while preserving picker Back/reopen behavior.\n- **Where:** es-app/src/guis/GuiWifi.cpp:470; es-app/src/guis/WifiScanProcess.h; es-app/src/main.cpp\n- **Why:** Detached worker owns the deadline and group cleanup; normal whole-ES exit can remove it with a blocked child outstanding. Historical picker-close proof did not cover process exit.\n- **Evidence:** Frozen source confirms no join/hook; inherited emustation.service uses KillMode=process. ES16dbac52 and focused observer/driver sources reviewed; original three-unit syntax, actual ES link and both driver builds pass (wifi-compiler-result-readback.md). Four GUI-free driver controls now have original observer1/0/0/0 and driver0 with candidate cleanup clear (audit-ui01-readback.md); the first actual GUI suite failed fixture navigation. Retry02 now directly verifies baseline normal-exit orphans and candidate clean join; Original1-second host-tool timing failed; narrow continuation now verifies59.060466ms complete-frame upper bound and same blocked scan on reopen, with normal exit/custody0 (audit-ui02-readback.md, wifi-back-reopen-readback.md).\n- **Acceptance:** Land exact ES source with required syntax check. Preserve an original known-bad normal-exit negative, candidate cancellation/atexit/completed-refresh results and actual frontend Back/reopen/SIGINT exit proof with exact child identities, no candidate forced cleanup and unchanged presentation. Document signal/fatal residual under D-CLOUD-133.\n\n## PL-006: Isolate the Steam runtime Python invocation\n\n- **Severity:** Low\n- **Category:** Code Quality\n- **Source Finding:** G-03 (external R-03)\n- **Owner area:** Steam runtime helper invocation\n- **What:** Use /usr/bin/python3 -I -S -B - for the self-contained runtime helper, matching all four sibling helpers.\n- **Where:** projects/ROCKNIX/packages/virtual/emulators/sources/Install Steam.sh:780\n- **Why:** Unisolated stdin Python admits cwd/module-path/site influence and PATH interpreter substitution after profile loading; no site dependency appears in the complete stdlib-only helper.\n- **Evidence:** Exact invocation/source comparison; shipped-profile searches do not eliminate ordinary Python import context. Actual installed-interpreter control reproduces old poisoned import failure and corrected successful whole synthetic transaction, with unchanged embedded body; see source-controls02-readback.md.\n- **Acceptance:** Land the one-line invocation with unchanged embedded body, preserve a bounded import-shadow old-negative/candidate-positive control and one narrow successful runtime-helper control using the installed interpreter. Keep broader native ARM qualification separate.\n\n## Pre-existing tracked scope (not punch items; exempt from Phase7 discovery gate)\n\n- #563 — source/licence custody for adopted artifacts and final composition acceptance; no blanket upstream hardware recertification.\n- #564/#579/#580/#582 — actual payload/installed ARM Steam/FEX/Proton/native/self-update boundaries, separate from passing synthetic full callers and exact installed-curl function proof.\n- #574/#575/#583/#584 — combined selected native engine, effective setting, gameplay/game-save/manual-state/automatic-state behavior and exact installed composition. Native03 ordinary Wii/Dreamcast cold game-save persistence is independently consumed in native-gameplay-supplement-readback.md; later f863 manual/automatic-state cases are independently accepted in native-state02-readback.md. Original source/coverage limits remain explicit.\n- #577 and public setup documentation tracking — current source/flow/frame binding plus separate public-doc publication; physical radio behavior excluded from controlled backend proof.\n- #349/#344/#511 and release/device issues — prior explicitly excluded restore/docs/device/publication work remains on its original tracker, not newly numbered by this audit.\n- #590 — final artifact/tracker/resolution closure. Audit completion cannot be inferred from this pre-issue list.\n\n## Leads resolved by review or retained as boundaries\n\nAll blind/refutation rows are preserved in04 and second-opinions readbacks. RVZ short-group speculation, normal persisted spaced Recent, missing OAuth cancel and the sanitizer-created unused-variable claim are refuted by source. Busy scans, conservative retained-card refusal, invalid stored country, manual recovery guidance, scan-input asymmetry, generated POT hygiene and repeated failed-RVZ cost are narrowed to their documented behaviors or coverage. F-10 profile reassignment is an explicit recorded restriction with environment overrides retained. R-02 slow-storage total-budget exhaustion is plausible but unverified as a defect; the finite global bound remains intentional. No silent dropped lead or extra runtime requirement is created.\n\n## Machine-readable index\n\n```yaml\npunch_index:\n\n- id: PL-001\n  severity: \"High\"\n  category: \"Interaction Defect\"\n  source_finding: \"F-002\"\n  owner_area: \"Dolphin package / default frontend\"\n  where: \"projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/standalone/dolphin-sa/patches/018-nogui-achievements-lifecycle.patch\"\n  acceptance: \"Land the guarded lifecycle patch, compile the actual target, and retain original actual-installed enabled/disabled/failed-boot lifecycle and loopback request/cleanup evidence. No real login, award or gameplay inference.\"\n  outcome: \"resolved\"\n\n- id: PL-002\n  severity: \"Medium\"\n  category: \"Code Quality\"\n  source_finding: \"F-001\"\n  owner_area: \"Steam installer\"\n  where: \"projects/ROCKNIX/packages/virtual/emulators/sources/Install Steam.sh:213\"\n  acceptance: \"Land the bounded exact function and preserve installed curl/Bash normal, declared-size oversize and stalled-response originals, exact argv, family-state equality and child cleanup.\"\n  outcome: \"resolved\"\n\n- id: PL-003\n  severity: \"Medium\"\n  category: \"Interaction Defect\"\n  source_finding: \"F-003\"\n  owner_area: \"Dolphin package installation\"\n  where: \"projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/standalone/dolphin-sa/package.mk\"\n  acceptance: \"Land the package alias, pass package checks/build, and retain exact installed link/resource identities plus absence of the four previous badge failures across enabled, disabled and boot-error startup controls.\"\n  outcome: \"resolved\"\n\n- id: PL-004\n  severity: \"Medium\"\n  category: \"Interaction Defect\"\n  source_finding: \"G-02 (external R-01)\"\n  owner_area: \"Dolphin helper and both native launchers\"\n  where: \"projects/ROCKNIX/packages/emulators/standalone/dolphin-sa/scripts/cheevos_dolphin.sh:21\"\n  acceptance: \"Two seeded-enabled-state transitions produce disabled/blank outputs with expected original1 and unchanged source settings. Failed publication preserves prior bytes and prevents both engines from launching with original error status; unchanged enabled routing and narrow EN/FR refusal flow/frame proof retained.\"\n  outcome: \"resolved\"\n\n- id: PL-005\n  severity: \"Low\"\n  category: \"Code Quality\"\n  source_finding: \"G-01 (external F-12b)\"\n  owner_area: \"ES Wi-Fi worker lifecycle\"\n  where: \"es-app/src/guis/GuiWifi.cpp:470; es-app/src/guis/WifiScanProcess.h; es-app/src/main.cpp\"\n  acceptance: \"Land exact ES source with required syntax check. Preserve an original known-bad normal-exit negative, candidate cancellation/atexit/completed-refresh results and actual frontend Back/reopen/SIGINT exit proof with exact child identities, no candidate forced cleanup and unchanged presentation. Document signal/fatal residual under D-CLOUD-133.\"\n  outcome: \"resolved\"\n\n- id: PL-006\n  severity: \"Low\"\n  category: \"Code Quality\"\n  source_finding: \"G-03 (external R-03)\"\n  owner_area: \"Steam runtime helper invocation\"\n  where: \"projects/ROCKNIX/packages/virtual/emulators/sources/Install Steam.sh:780\"\n  acceptance: \"Land the one-line invocation with unchanged embedded body, preserve a bounded import-shadow old-negative/candidate-positive control and one narrow successful runtime-helper control using the installed interpreter. Keep broader native ARM qualification separate.\"\n  outcome: \"resolved\"\n\n```\n\n## Phase 7 resolution gate\n\nThis table records verified outcomes available at creation; all six punch outcomes are resolved within their stated scopes. Phase6 tracker #596 and live update04 are verified; checkpoint resolution lints passed. Final selected clean/retained composition is accepted. The later four-launch native-state proof is independently accepted. All seven audit phases are complete; root owns final tracker/artifact publication and any cadence record. This is not RC approval. A source-only proposal is not Resolved.\n\n| Item | Outcome | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| PL-001 | Resolved | Resolved in `9aaaaa0f642b97ebf722c2e1aeedb7e4d00bcbdc`, present in d4af and next by direct branch/read checks. `dolphin-installed-supplement-readback.md` verifies original installed evidence. G-02 is a separate retained-settings defect, not a reason to erase this lifecycle correction. |\n| PL-002 | Resolved | Resolved in `9aaaaa0f642b97ebf722c2e1aeedb7e4d00bcbdc`; exact metadata control/readback in `steam-supplement-readback.json` and durable Steam remaining result. Undeclared-length size enforcement is not claimed; total time remains bounded. No installed ARM Steam claim. |\n| PL-003 | Resolved | Resolved in `6616cc36cb85d86878870feafdcb64edbc192df8` under #592, present in d4af/next; engineering-image and dolphin-installed supplemental readbacks directly verify originals. No claim every Sys consumer was separately exercised. |\n| PL-004 | Resolved | Resolved in `d9054efc463387df3f0211481c5ae8c793dfadc8` on feature/m7-player-setup under #594. All15 helper/exact caller-block controls plus actual full Wii/runemu/ES intended EN/FR refusal at640/1280 and exact original config restoration verified (audit-ui1280-02-readback.md). Those flow controls used explicit candidate overlays. Final f863 untouched/retained continuations additionally verify actual installed full helper/exact launcher blocks with synthetic engine markers, source-preservation checks and original exits; see final-clean-affec